{"name":"Love Poem","hex":"#a06582","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"love","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep caring for the existence of another.","Strong affection."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have a strong affection for (someone or something).","To need, thrive on."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/love"},{"term":"poem","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A literary piece written in verse.","A piece of writing in the tradition of poetry, an instance of poetry."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poem"}],"entries":[{"title":"Love Poem (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Love Poem\" is a song by South Korean singer-songwriter IU, released by Kakao M as the lead single from her seventh Korean-language EP Love Poem on November 1, 2019. It debuted at number 11 on the Gaon Digital Chart before topping the chart the following week, becoming IU's 21st number-one single in South Korea, and extending her record for the most number ones on the chart."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7c/IU_-_Love_Poem.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love_Poem_(song)","wikidata":"Q75128079"},{"title":"Love Poem (EP)","blocks":[{"text":"Love Poem is the fifth Korean-language extended play by South Korean singer-songwriter IU. The EP was released on November 18, 2019, through Kakao M. It includes the lead single and title track, \"Love Poem\", as well as the tracks \"Above the Time\" and \"Blueming\", which both received music videos. The EP debuted atop the Gaon Album Chart, selling over 168,000 copies in South Korea in November 2019 and had been certified platinum by the Korean Music Content Association for selling over 250,000 copies."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f1/IU_-_Love_Poem_EP.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love_Poem_(EP)","wikidata":"Q76961040"},{"title":"Poetry","blocks":[{"text":"Poetry is a form of literary art that uses aesthetic and often rhythmic qualities of language to evoke meanings in addition to, or in place of, literal or surface-level meanings. A particular instance of poetry is a poem and is written by a poet. Poets use a variety of techniques called poetic devices, such as assonance, alliteration, consonance, euphony and cacophony, onomatopoeia, rhythm, rhyme schemes and sound symbolism, to produce musical or other artistic effects. They also frequently organize these devices into poetic structures, which may be strict or loose, conventional or invented by the poet. Poetic structures vary dramatically by language and cultural convention, but they often rely on rhythmic metre: patterns of syllable stress or syllable weight. They may also use repeating patterns of phonemes, phoneme groups, tones, words, or entire phrases. Poetic structures may even be semantic."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poetry","wikidata":"Q482"},{"title":"Love","blocks":[{"text":"Love encompasses a range of strong and positive emotional and mental states, from the most sublime virtue or good habit, the deepest interpersonal affection, to the simplest pleasure. An example of this range of meanings is that the love of a mother differs from the love of a spouse, which differs from the love for food. Most commonly, love refers to a feeling of strong attraction and emotional attachment."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love","wikidata":"Q316"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Books_and_Scroll_Ornament_with_Open_Book.png/500px-Books_and_Scroll_Ornament_with_Open_Book.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Books_and_Scroll_Ornament_with_Open_Book.png/500px-Books_and_Scroll_Ornament_with_Open_Book.